# Optional. m8 runs without a .env file: you give it the Gemini key on the setup
# screen, and the server stores it sealed in its database. You can set these in
# the shell instead, for example `PORT=4000 bun run dev`.

# The port apps/server listens on. apps/web/vite.config.ts proxies to it in
# development. `bun run start --port 4000` does the same.
# PORT=3001

# Where apps/server listens: every interface by default, so a phone on the same
# network can reach it. `bun run start --host 127.0.0.1` does the same.
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# Set this before the server is reachable by anybody else, through a tunnel for
# example. The page asks for it once per browser. Without it anyone with the URL
# can open sessions on your Gemini key and read what he remembers.
# At least 12 characters. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 18
# M8_ACCESS_KEY=

# Where his memory is kept. One SQLite file, created on first start.
# The default is data/m8.sqlite in the repository, which git ignores.
# MEMORY_DB_PATH=

# Where the key that seals the stored Gemini key is kept. Generated on first
# start with mode 0600. It must not be inside the database's directory. Back it
# up apart from the database: without it the stored Gemini key does not open.
# The default is keys/ in the repository, which git ignores.
# M8_KEYS_DIR=

# Development only: for reaching the dev server from a phone through an https
# reverse proxy of your own. Browsers refuse the camera and the microphone on
# plain http. Set these in the shell, not here, unless you always work that way.
# M8_DEV_HTTPS=1                  the hot-reload socket uses wss on 443
# M8_DEV_HOSTS=.example.dev       hostnames the dev server answers to, comma separated
